=E2=80=8Bla gleki di'e ciska:
=E2=80=8B
=E2=80=8B

>
>
> Em sexta-feira, 29 de julho de 2016 11:57:49 UTC+3, la uakci escreveu:
>

=E2=80=8BWhat language is this header in?



> coi jbozabna
>>
>> In Lojban, all tanru are made by putting two (or more; technically one
>> brivla also
>> makes for a tanru, but anyway) brivla next to each other.
>>
>> I'm considering something of a dialect/preference/whatever that would
>> require a tanru
>> to be enclosed in {ke} to make it a tanru; otherwise, it would break int=
o
>> two selbri.
>> For example, {lo blanu stizu} would parse as {<lo blanu KU> [CU stizu
>> VAU]}
>>
>
> Maybe instead use alternatives to LE?
> E.g.
> {.i blanu bu stizu} already works like that.
>

=E2=80=8BGood point, but while {bu} eats one word, *hypothetical cmavo* sho=
uld eat
one selbrisle.
(Of course assuming that a {ke}-{ke'e} =E2=80=8Bbracket counts as selbrisle=
.)



>
>
>
>> , and to
>> express the intended 'blue chair', it'd be required to say {lo ke blanu
>> stizu}.
>>
>
> How would tanru containing >=3D3 selbrisle work? Would {lo blanu broda
> broda} parse as {lo blanu cu broda broda}?
>

=E2=80=8BThat wouldn't parse here. Think about it in terms of a grammar:

    jufra =3D sumti* selbri sumti* / sumti*
    sumti =3D LE selbri
    selbri =3D KE brivla* KEhE? / brivla

{lo blanu stizu} parses as:

jufra
|
+---------+
|         |
sumti     selbri
|         |
+--+      brivla
|  |      |
LE selbri |
|  |      |
|  brivla |
|  |      |
=3D=3D =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D  =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
lo blanu  stizu
(regular Lojban: lo blanu cu stizu)

(Apologies for the cheesy ASCII tree, but anyways.)

{lo ke blanu stizu}:

jufra
|
sumti
|
+--+
|  |
LE selbri
|  |
|  +--+------+
|  |  |      |
|  KE brivla brivla
|  |  |      |
=3D=3D =3D=3D =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D  =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
lo ke blanu  stizu
(regular: lo blanu cu stizu)

Your {lo blanu broda broda} doesn't parse - it'd parse to this point:

jufra
|
+---------+------+
|         |      |
sumti     selbri sumti
|         |      |
+--+      brivla LE
|  |      |      |
LE selbri |      |
|  |      |      |
|  brivla |      |
|  |      |      |
=3D=3D =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D  =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D  =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
lo blanu  broda  broda!?

That doesn't match (as you can see), since {broda} isn't among the selma'o
BRIVLA
(let's pretend BRIVLA is a selma'o).

If we add NU, then your proposed thingy would work in context.
It's also possible for an unmatching brivla to start a new bridi, with the
{.i} elided:

    selsku =3D (I* jufra)*

Then:

selsku
|
+----------------+
|                |
jufra            jufra
|                |
+---------+      selbri
|         |      |
sumti     selbri brivla
|         |      |
+--+      brivla |
|  |      |      |
LE selbri |      |
|  |      |      |
|  brivla |      |
|  |      |      |
=3D=3D =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D  =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D  =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
lo blanu  broda  broda
(regular: lo blanu cu broda .i broda)

Hope it makes sense.

~ mi'e la uakci mu'o re'i
  .i .e'e ma'a jbokei gi'e nai jboke'i ~


